[0.003, "o", "\u001b[24;1H\u001b[38;5;248m\u001b[48;5;255m\u276f \u001b[38;5;16mOK cool. Let's take this for a spin with some tests. What would a test harness look like to send one of our sample receipts in \u001b[39m   \u001b[25;1H  \u001b[38;5;16mand check the output?\u001b[39m                                                                                                             \u001b[26;1H                                                                                                                                    \u001b[27;1H  \u001b[38;5;16mIs there helpful stuff we can extract from what we wrote for eval? What's a good predicate for a first test of receipt parsing?\u001b[39m   \u001b[28;3H\u001b[49m  \u001b[C     \u001b[C       \u001b[C     \u001b[C  \u001b[C   \u001b[C       \u001b[C    \u001b[C    \u001b[C  \u001b[C     \u001b[C   \u001b[C     \u001b[C      \u001b[C \u001b[C    \u001b[C         \u001b[C   \u001b[C \u001b[C     \u001b[C    \u001b[C  \u001b[C       \u001b[C         \r\n\u001b[38;5;174m\u273d\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;216mIm\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;174mprovising\u2026 \u001b[39m                                                                                                               "]
