[0.003, "o", "\u001b[28;1H\u001b[38;5;248m\u001b[48;5;255m\u276f \u001b[38;5;16mThis is pretty reasonable. Some feedback before we commit to it:\u001b[39m                                                                  \u001b[29;1H                                                                                                                                    \u001b[30;1H  \u001b[38;5;16m- The templated strings for error messages seem a bit overkill. Is there not an assertEquals we can use?\u001b[39m                          \u001b[31;1H  \u001b[38;5;16m- Also, the custom main() was fine for the little eval we set up. For this, though, a test framework seems better because we're \u001b[39m  \u001b[32;1H  \u001b[38;5;16mrewriting a lot of reporting. Suggest a straightforward framework for this, please\u001b[39m                                                \u001b[33;3H\u001b[49m         \u001b[C \u001b[C   \u001b[C  \u001b[C          \u001b[C       \u001b[C \u001b[C               \u001b[C         \u001b[C   \u001b[C     \u001b[C       \r\n\u001b[38;5;174m\u273d\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mStewing\u2026 \u001b[39m                                                                               "]
